.TH LLCV 1 "2026-10-07" "LLCV 2.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llcv \- low-latency viewer for USB HDMI capture devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llcv
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llcv
shows video and audio from UVC (V4L2) HDMI capture devices with minimal
delay. Video is captured with V4L2 memory-mapped buffers, only the newest
frame is presented with OpenGL, and capture audio is played through the
system audio server (PipeWire) with a small drift-corrected buffer.
.PP
The settings screen selects the capture device, resolution, pixel format,
frame rate, audio devices and window behavior. Settings are stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/llcv/settings.ini .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-x11
Use the X11 backend (XWayland on Wayland sessions) for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-wayland
Use the Wayland backend for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Show the settings screen even when it is configured to be skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-sdr
Disable HDR output and the 10-bit framebuffer for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Alt
Show or hide the menu bar.
.TP
.B F1
App information and shortcuts.
.TP
.B F2
Stop playback and open the settings screen.
.TP
.B F3
Audio meters and volume controls.
.TP
.B F5
Restore the 1:1 source size.
.TP
.BR F11 ", " Alt+Enter
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B F12
Save a PNG screenshot at the capture resolution.
.TP
.B Tab
Live diagnostics.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave fullscreen, or exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/llcv/settings.ini
User settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/llcv/logs/llcv.log
Diagnostic log, when enabled.
.TP
.I $XDG_PICTURES_DIR/LLCV/
Screenshots.
.SH HDR
P010 (10-bit HDR10) capture needs Linux 7.1 or newer, or a uvcvideo module
with P010 support. On Wayland compositors that offer the
wp_color_management_v1 protocol (GNOME 48 and later, KDE Plasma 6), HDR10
input is passed through to HDR displays. Otherwise HDR10 is tone mapped to
SDR. X11 always uses tone mapping.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR v4l2-ctl (1)
